  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material describing the sensory joke",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) which uses the first-person plural 'my wife' and the second-person 'you' to create an immersive, participatory experience. The phrase 'if you put your ear to it' directly addresses the viewer, inviting them to imagine themselves performing the action described, thereby projecting the user onto the textual instruction. The user is also implicitly projected onto the visual material (legs) as the subject of the action ('my wife') and the object of the sensory experience ('you can smell the ocean'), making the user feel personally involved in the absurd scenario.",
